Modification of Dijkstra's Algorithm for Shortest Path
Calculation
Problem Statement
Dijkstra's algorithm is used to find the shortest distances between vertices in a
weighted graph. Modify the program to perform the following operations:
A. Select a different source vertex and recalculate the shortest distances.
B. Display the complete shortest path to a destination vertex, not only its distance.
C. Update an edge weight and recalculate the shortest paths.
